@startuml
title Create KNN Lookup Sequence (/knn/{slug}/save and /api/admin/knn/{slug})

autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Admin
boundary "Create KNN UI" as CreateKnnUi
control "KnnController\n(FE Dashboard)" as FeController
control "AdminKnnController\n(BE API)" as BeController
entity "AgeRange / Region /\nOccupation / EducationLevel /\nLearningPurpose\n(FE Response DTO)" as FeLookupDto
entity "CreateAgeRangeRequest / CreateRegionRequest /\nCreateOccupationRequest / CreateEducationLevelRequest /\nCreateLearningPurposeRequest\n(BE Request DTO)" as BeCreateDto
entity "AgeRangeResponse / RegionResponse /\nOccupationResponse / EducationLevelResponse /\nLearningPurposeResponse\n(BE Response DTO)" as BeLookupResponseDto
control "AdminKnnLookupService" as LookupService
entity "AgeRange" as AgeRangeEntity
entity "Region" as RegionEntity
entity "Occupation" as OccupationEntity
entity "EducationLevel" as EducationLevelEntity
entity "LearningPurpose" as LearningPurposeEntity
control "AdminKnnLookupRepository" as LookupRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL

note over CreateKnnUi, MySQL
Checked in current code:
Dashboard UI file exists: Views/Knn/Lookup.cshtml.
FE controller exists: KnnController.
FE response DTOs exist: AgeRange, Region, Occupation, EducationLevel and LearningPurpose.
BE controller exists: AdminKnnController.
BE create request DTOs and response DTOs exist for each KNN lookup type.
Create KNN means creating one lookup row under age-ranges, regions, occupations,
education-levels or learning-purposes.
Entities exist: AgeRange, Region, Occupation, EducationLevel and LearningPurpose.
end note

Admin -> CreateKnnUi: Enter lookup fields
Admin -> CreateKnnUi: Save new lookup item
CreateKnnUi -> FeController: POST /knn/{slug}/save\nid = 0, form data
FeController -> FeController: Validate slug\nand build payload
FeController -> BeController: VocaNovaApiClient.CreateKnnLookupAsync\nPOST /api/admin/knn/{slug}
BeController -> BeCreateDto: Bind request body\nby slug
BeCreateDto --> BeController: Create lookup request
BeController -> BeController: Check admin authorization
BeController -> BeController: Validate create request

alt Request invalid
    BeController --> FeController: HTTP 400 error
    FeController --> CreateKnnUi: Show error message
else Request valid
    BeController -> LookupService: Create{LookupType}Async(command)
    LookupService -> LookupService: Normalize and validate fields
    LookupService -> LookupRepository: Check duplicate name/code
    LookupRepository -> DbContext: Query lookup table
    DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT age_ranges / regions /\noccupations / education_levels /\nlearning_purposes
    MySQL --> DbContext: Duplicate row or null
    DbContext --> LookupRepository: Duplicate check result
    LookupRepository --> LookupService: exists or not

    alt Duplicate or invalid parent
        LookupService --> BeController: Conflict or validation failure
        BeController --> FeController: HTTP 400/409 error
        FeController --> CreateKnnUi: Show error message
    else Lookup item can be created
        LookupService -> LookupRepository: Create lookup row
        LookupRepository -> AgeRangeEntity: Create AgeRange if slug age-ranges
        LookupRepository -> RegionEntity: Create Region if slug regions
        LookupRepository -> OccupationEntity: Create Occupation if slug occupations
        LookupRepository -> EducationLevelEntity: Create EducationLevel if slug education-levels
        LookupRepository -> LearningPurposeEntity: Create LearningPurpose if slug learning-purposes
        AgeRangeEntity --> LookupRepository: AgeRange?
        RegionEntity --> LookupRepository: Region?
        OccupationEntity --> LookupRepository: Occupation?
        EducationLevelEntity --> LookupRepository: EducationLevel?
        LearningPurposeEntity --> LookupRepository: LearningPurpose?
        LookupRepository -> DbContext: Add lookup entity
        DbContext -> MySQL: INSERT lookup table
        MySQL --> DbContext: Insert result
        DbContext --> LookupRepository: Saved lookup
        LookupRepository --> LookupService: Created lookup item
        LookupService --> BeController: Created lookup result
        BeController -> BeLookupResponseDto: Create lookup response
        BeLookupResponseDto --> BeController: Lookup response
        BeController -> FeLookupDto: HTTP 201 Created\nlookup response JSON
        FeLookupDto --> FeController: Lookup DTO
        FeController --> CreateKnnUi: Show created feedback
    end
end

@enduml
